A||N||4||DaveL||87 2.5 Automatic Trans mount||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||10-30-2000||09:15 AM||||Well, the motor mount finally took a dump on my 87. Had a hard time locating a mount, ended up going back to GM. $80 later I have a mount. While I was there, I decided to check the price and availability of the trans. mount, and he said it is no longer available from GM.....If the motor mount went, then I think the tranny mount can't be too far behind. Is there any place to find this mount? As I understand it, in this year (87) with a 2.5 auto, there is only 1 tranny mount, and 1 engine mount??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||10-30-2000||03:42 PM||||You can get the transmission mount from almost any Advance Auto or other auto parts store.  They are not listed in the computer, but ask for #M2543. I found it by looking through the printed catalogs at the store.  The one I got was from L&S Automotive Products, but I have been told that you can cross reference the number to several brands.<P>I would stongly suggest that you replace the dogbone when you replace these mounts.  The 2 mount system puts a lot of stress on the dogbone and wears it out quickly.  See the info in the Orgre's Cave for more info. <P>Engine side mounts are still available for the 2.5L motors, just ask for a engine (front) mount for a 88 Pontiac 6000 with the 2.5L motor.  The mounts are the same and much easier to find.<P>Bob<BR>2-87 GT's<BR>87 Coupe<BR>85 SE (For Sale)<P><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000002||theogre||10-30-2000||07:38 PM||||By all means check the tranny mount. Don't be suprised if it's in allot better shape than the motor mount. The motor mount get oil dumped into it from filer changes and such. My motor mount is shot but my tranny mount is pretty decent.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mbramble||10-31-2000||07:47 AM||||Tranny mounts (and motor mounts, etc.) are available from the Fiero Store.  I ordered on Mon. had them on Thur.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DaveL||10-31-2000||07:49 AM||||What a difference!!! The trany mount looked OK. At first, though, it still made a slight clunk when I put it into reverse. Looking at the dogbone, I see it isn't centered in the adjustment slot. Could that cause a slight clunk??? I also had a new EGR valve put on, and that has almost eliminated the annoying tick I was getting.||||reg||3
